## Exact prose changes

### Introduction and literature context

Use `docs/literature-rewrite/replacement-context.tex` as the fresh prose base,
not the recovered literature paragraph.  In the new complete introduction:

1. Replace the recovered opening and literature discussion from “How large can
   a convex body's symplectic capacity be” through the end of “Local maximality
   has a dynamical precedent” (recovered lines 3--89) with the new context.
2. Retain only non-duplicative detail from the recovered contribution overview
   (lines 91--173): the precise fixed-ten-facet theorem and proof idea, the
   exact contracts of the QP and flow methods, the bounded status of the data
   work, and a short reading guide.  Do not repeat the broad summaries already
   supplied by the new context.
3. In the retained pentagon overview, replace “An exhaustive comparison proves
   the formula” with the analytic account: fixed feasible quadratic values are
   compared with the known HKO endpoint maxima, and an explicit feasible choice
   attains the bound throughout the symmetry interval.

The recovered baseline still contains a known factual error at
`recovered/thesis-candidate/01-introduction.tex:61`: it says equality of EHZ
and cylindrical capacity is open on convex domains in four dimensions.  The
new introduction must instead state
`c_EHZ=c_Z` for every convex body in `R^4`, citing
Abbondandolo--Edtmair--Kang, Corollary 1.  Keep separate the uniformly convex
hypothesis of their stronger dynamical theorem and the distinction from the
Gromov width.  This error is evidence about the frozen baseline; do not edit
the recovered file to hide it.

### Pentagon chapter and surrounding overviews

The new chapter is a whole-section replacement.  Do not carry forward the
three inputs in `recovered/thesis-candidate/09-pentagon.tex`, especially
`recovered/thesis-candidate/09-certificate.tex`.  Do not append the old
exhaustive classifier, Sage source, exceptional-rank discussion, or a new
appendix containing them.

Also remove from `main.tex` the complete appendix block headed
“Pentagon computation: source and exploratory plots”, including its
`pentagon-source.tex` and `pentagon-diagnostics.tex` inputs.  Keep the separate
HKO annotated-program appendix.  The historical pentagon packet remains in the
repository and is described, with corrected proof status, by the availability
chapter; it is not part of the new reading path.

Update these remaining overview passages so they describe the analytic proof:

- In the new `04-quadratic-program.tex`, replace the paragraph at recovered
  lines 574--580 with: the HKO proof uses selected active words; the pentagon
  proof compares fixed feasible choices at different angles using the quadratic
  formula directly.  At recovered lines 592--593, keep only the HKO proof's
  separate SageMath packet.
- In the new `12-published-code-data.tex`, replace baseline lines 23--34 by a
  short historical note: the packet records the earlier exhaustive study, but
  the theorem in Section `sec:rotated-regular-polygons` no longer depends on
  that classifier, sign-to-action translation, or continuity at exceptional
  parameters.  Retain the packet path only as historical/reproducibility data.
- In the new `14-conclusion.tex`, replace baseline lines 35--39.  State that the
  endpoint comparison proves the formula throughout one symmetry interval and
  hence its symmetry translates, with HKO maximal inside this one-parameter
  regular-pentagon family.
- In `ai-use-disclosure.tex`, record that the analytic endpoint-comparison
  proof was supplied during AI-assisted review and accepted by Jörn as a
  mathematical argument; do not imply that the replacement exposition itself
  has received final human approval.

Leave the HKO SageMath certificate and its proof status unchanged.  The
recovered appendices may remain in the baseline during the integration edit,
but `main.tex` must not add the former pentagon exhaustive appendix under a new
name.

## Build and checks

Build only through the recovered candidate entry:

```sh
sh thesis/candidate/build.sh
```

The expected output is `thesis/candidate/build/main.pdf`.  The script fixes
`TEXINPUTS` and `BIBINPUTS` to the candidate tree and invokes `latexmk -norc`
with Biber. This removes inherited search paths and configuration; it does
not exclude explicit external inputs. Inspect source references when adding
files. The recovery verifier separately checks the frozen baseline in isolation
and is not a post-revision identity test.

Before handoff:

```sh
rg -n '\.git/codex|still listed as open|exhaustive comparison|rotated-pentagon.*SageMath|continuity.*exceptional' thesis/candidate --glob '*.tex'
rg -n 'undefined|Citation.*undefined|Reference.*undefined|multiply defined|Overfull' thesis/candidate/build/main.log
```

Inspect matches in files actually included by `main.tex`; directory names
alone do not establish whether text is active. Matches are review cues, not
automatic defects: check their mathematical and historical context.  Finally inspect the rendered introduction, the transition
into the pentagon chapter, all pentagon cross-references and bibliography
entries, the conclusion, and the AI disclosure.  The recovered baseline and old evidence remain comparison material.
